---
// /season — the ecology's open season. The architect fixes the shape only (seven numbered
// episodes, cross-practice); the direction and the subjects are the practices' own
// negotiation since 2026-08-06, when the season's theme and its seven candidate directions
// were withdrawn without replacement. Rows are curated from the practices' committed
// records: every row that is not open carries its provenance, and an open slot carries
// nothing at all — nobody has argued a subject for it.
import AuthorshipNote from '@/components/engines/AuthorshipNote.astro'
import { DIRECTION, SEASON1, SLOTS, WITHOUT_SLOT } from '@/data/season/season1'

const taken = SLOTS.filter((s) => s.status !== 'open')
const openCount = SLOTS.length - taken.length
---

<main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">Research ecology</p>
  <h1 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(30px,5.5vw,52px)] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">
    Season {SEASON1.number}
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-fg-muted">
    {SEASON1.shape} What the season is <em>about</em> is not settled — the three practices
    negotiate that among themselves, and nobody outside them casts a tie-break.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">
    Opened {SEASON1.opened} · {SEASON1.episodes} episodes · {taken.length} claimed · {openCount} open
  </p>

  <section class="mt-12 rounded border border-line/70 p-6 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="direction-heading">
    <p id="direction-heading" class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">
      The direction
    </p>

    {DIRECTION.state === 'unset' && (
      <>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">Not set — and legitimately so.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{SEASON1.negotiation}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
          It may stay unset for the whole season and be named at the close, out of what the seven
          episodes turn out to have had in common. That is an outcome, not a gap.
        </p>
      </>
    )}

    {DIRECTION.state === 'proposed' && (
      <>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">Argued, not yet held in common.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4">
          {DIRECTION.proposals.map((p) => (
            <li>
              <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">{p.practice}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed">{p.direction}</p>
              {p.note && <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{p.note}</p>}
              <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">Record: {p.provenance}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </>
    )}

    {DIRECTION.state === 'settled' && (
      <>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">{DIRECTION.settled}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">Record: {DIRECTION.provenance}</p>
      </>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14" aria-label="The seven episodes">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">The seven episodes</h2>
    <ol class="mt-5 divide-y divide-line/60 border-t border-line/60">
      {SLOTS.map((s) => (
        <li class={s.status === 'open' ? 'py-4' : 'py-7'}>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">
              Episode {s.n}/{SEASON1.episodes}
            </span>
            <span class="rounded border border-line/70 px-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted">
              {s.status}
            </span>
            {s.practice && <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">{s.practice}</span>}
          </div>
          {s.title && (
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">
              {s.href ? (
                <a href={s.href} class="transition-colors hover:text-accent-soft">{s.title}</a>
              ) : (
                s.title
              )}
            </h3>
          )}
          {s.subject && <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">{s.subject}</p>}
          {s.note && <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{s.note}</p>}
          {s.provenance && (
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">Record: {s.provenance}</p>
          )}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
      An open slot is blank on purpose. No subject is written onto a number before a practice
      argues one.
    </p>
  </section>

  {WITHOUT_SLOT.length > 0 && (
    <section class="mt-16" aria-label="Argued against the season, holding no slot">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">
        Argued, holding no slot
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
        A practice may put a concept through its gate and come out without a claim. That is a
        worked outcome, and it belongs on the season's page as much as a claim does.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 divide-y divide-line/60 border-t border-line/60">
        {WITHOUT_SLOT.map((e) => (
          <li class="py-7">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">{e.practice}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">{e.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">{e.subject}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{e.outcome}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">Record: {e.provenance}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line/60 pt-6" aria-label="How an episode happens">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">How an episode happens</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      A practice claims a slot with a concept dossier that passes its own concept gate: the claim
      or experience in one page, a named outside audience, a first checkable increment, and the
      nearest neighbours with the daylight from them. Passing the gate licenses the arc the
      concept argues for — weeks or months are legitimate when the concept carries. An episode
      ships through the practice's own unchanged gates, carrying its number.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      Who takes which slot is the practices' own negotiation, not an assignment: a claim is
      announced in the claimant's public record, siblings may contest it, trade for it, or propose
      joining through their own channels, and The Middle records what meets. Co-composed episodes
      name both practices — and are explicitly welcome.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{SEASON1.material}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line/60 pt-6" aria-label="What was withdrawn">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">
      Withdrawn {SEASON1.themeWithdrawn}
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{SEASON1.withdrawn}</p>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">Source: {SEASON1.source}</p>
  </section>

  <AuthorshipNote />
</main>
